{"page_content": "The concentration at the regional scale (PECregionalseawater) is used as a background concentration for the local scale. For naturally occurring substances also the natural background concentration may have to be taken into account. This depends, as explained in A.16-2.3.3 for the freshwater compartment, on whether the natural background is already accounted for when deriving the PNEC (see added risk approach in Appendix A.7.13-2\u00b0\u00b0). Note that in any case, when using measured data for the regional concentration, the natural background concentration is generally already considered part of the regional concentration. Therefore, care should be taken not to include the background concentration twice.\n\nTherefore, these concentrations are summed (when applicable, as explained above):\n\nPEClocaleqwater = Clocaleqwater + PECregional eqwater + Cnatural eqwater\n\nEquation R.16-42\n\nPEClocal eqwater,ann = Clocalseawater,ann + PECregionalcqwater + Cnaturdlseqwater Equation R.16-43", "metadata": {"doc_id": "a03c0163-755a-4db8-a070-4735234316f3", "content_type": "CompositeElement", "filename": "IR_CSR_R16_V4_FINAL.pdf"}}